ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":162,"index":162,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 8, end: 9 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"1. Introduction "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":163,"index":163,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 9, end: 12 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"This Standard defines methods for digital signature generation that can be used for the protection of binary data (commonly called a message), and for the verification and validation of those digital signatures. Three techniques are approved. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":164,"index":164,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 12, end: 13 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"(1) The Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA) is specified in this Standard. The specification "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":165,"index":165,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 13, end: 15 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"includes criteria for the generation of domain parameters, for the generation of public and private key pairs, and for the generation and verification of digital signatures. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":166,"index":166,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 15, end: 16 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"(2) The RSA digital signature algorithm is specified in American National Standard (ANS) "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":167,"index":167,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 16, end: 19 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"X9.31 and Public Key Cryptography Standard (PKCS) #1. FIPS 186-4 approves the use of implementations of either or both of these standards and specifies additional requirements. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":168,"index":168,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 19, end: 20 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"(3) The Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) is specified in ANS X9.62. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":169,"index":169,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 20, end: 22 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"FIPS 186-4 approves the use of ECDSA and specifies additional requirements. Recommended elliptic curves for Federal Government use are provided herein. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":170,"index":170,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 22, end: 24 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"This Standard includes requirements for obtaining the assurances necessary for valid digital signatures. Methods for obtaining these assurances are provided in NIST Special Publication "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":171,"index":171,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(16), start: 24, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[10],"side":0,"text":"(SP) 800-89, Recommendation for Obtaining Assurances for Digital Signature Applications. "}
