ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":961,"index":961,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 4, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"A.2 Generation of the Generator g "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":962,"index":962,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 5, end: 16 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"The generator g depends on the values of p and q. Two methods for determining the generator g are provided; one of these methods shall be used. The first method, discussed in Appendix A.2.1, may be used when complete validation of the generator g is not required; it is recommended that this method be used only when the party generating g is trusted to not deliberately generate a g that has a potentially exploitable relationship to another generator g′. For example, it must be hard to determine an exponential relationship between the generators such that g = (g′)x mod p for a known value of x. (Note: Read (g′)x as g prime to the x.) Appendix A.2.2 provides a method for partial validation when the method of generation in Appendix A.2.1 is used. The second method for generating g, discussed in Appendix A.2.3, shall be used when validation of the generator g is required; the method for the validation of a generator determined using the method in Appendix A.2.3 is provided in Appendix A.2.4. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":963,"index":963,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 16, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"A.2.1 Unverifiable Generation of the Generator g "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":964,"index":964,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 17, end: 22 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"This method is used to determine a value for g, based on the values of p and q. It may be used when validation of the generator g is not required. The correct generation of g cannot be completely validated (see Appendix A.2.2). Note that this generation method for g was also specified in previous versions of this Standard. The following process or its equivalent shall be used to generate the generator g for this method. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":965,"index":965,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 22, end: 23 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"Input: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":966,"index":966,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 23, end: 24 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"1. p, q The generated primes. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":967,"index":967,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 24, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"Output: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":968,"index":968,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 25, end: 26 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"1. g The requested value of g. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":969,"index":969,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(113), start: 26, end: 27 })","issues":"[]","pages":[50],"side":0,"text":"Process: "}
