ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1204,"index":1204,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 23, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":" In addition, all IFC keys shall meet the following criteria in order to conform to FIPS 186-4: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1205,"index":1205,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 25, end: 26 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":"1. The public exponent e shall be selected with the following constraints: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1206,"index":1206,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 26, end: 27 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":"(a) The public verification exponent e shall be selected prior to generating the primes "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1207,"index":1207,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 27, end: 28 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":"p and q, and the private signature exponent d. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1208,"index":1208,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 28, end: 29 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":"(b) The exponent e shall be an odd positive integer such that: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1209,"index":1209,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 29, end: 30 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":" 216 < e < 2256. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1210,"index":1210,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 30, end: 32 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":"Note that the value of e may be any value that meets constraint 1(b), i.e., e may be either a fixed value or a random value. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1211,"index":1211,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 32, end: 33 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":" 2. The primes p and q shall be selected with the following constraints: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1212,"index":1212,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 33, end: 35 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":"(a) (p–1) and (q–1) shall be relatively prime to the public exponent e. (b) The private prime factor p shall be selected randomly and shall satisfy "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1213,"index":1213,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(128), start: 35, end: 38 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":0,"text":" and len(q). In each case, len(p) = len(q) = nlen/2.  "}
