ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1219,"index":1219,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 2, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"desired security_strength. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1220,"index":1220,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 3, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"(c) The private prime factor q shall be selected randomly and shall satisfy "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1221,"index":1221,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 4, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"( 2 )(2(nlen / 2) – 1) ≤ q ≤ (2nlen / 2– 1), where nlen is the appropriate length for the "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1222,"index":1222,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 5, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"desired security_strength. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1223,"index":1223,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 6, end: 7 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"(d) |p – q| > 2(nlen / 2) – 100. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1224,"index":1224,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 7, end: 9 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"3. The private signature exponent d shall be selected with the following constraints after the generation of p and q: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1225,"index":1225,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 9, end: 10 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"(a) The exponent d shall be a positive integer value such that "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1226,"index":1226,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 10, end: 11 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"2nlen/ 2 < d < LCM(p–1, q–1), and "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1227,"index":1227,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 11, end: 12 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"(b) d = e–1 mod (LCM(p–1, q–1)). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1228,"index":1228,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 12, end: 13 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"That is, the inequality in (a) holds, and 1 ≡ (ed) (mod LCM(p–1, q–1)). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1229,"index":1229,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 13, end: 15 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"In the extremely rare event that d ≤ 2nlen / 2, then new values for p, q and d shall be determined. A different value of e may be used, although this is not required. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1230,"index":1230,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 15, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"Any hash function used during the generation of the key pair shall be approved (i.e., specified in FIPS 180). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1231,"index":1231,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 17, end: 18 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"B.3.2 Generation of Random Primes that are Provably Prime "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1232,"index":1232,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 18, end: 24 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"An approved method that satisfies the constraints of Appendix B.3.1 shall be used for the generation of IFC random primes p and q that are provably prime (see case A.1). One such method is provided in Appendix B.3.2.1 and B.3.2.2. For this method, a random seed is initially required (see Appendix B.3.2.1); the length of the seed is equal to twice the security strength associated with the modulus n. After the seed is obtained, the primes can be generated (see Appendix B.3.2.2). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1233,"index":1233,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(129), start: 24, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[62],"side":0,"text":"B.3.2.1 Get the Seed "}
