ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1772,"index":1772,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 2, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"Notes: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1773,"index":1773,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 3, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"1. By starting with X0 > (1/2) Sqrt(C), X0 − Sqrt(C)is guaranteed to be less than X0 . "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1774,"index":1774,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 4, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"This inequality is maintained in step 5; i.e., Xi − Sqrt(C)< Xi for all i. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1775,"index":1775,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 5, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"2. For i ≥ 1, 0 ≤ Xi − Sqrt(C) = (Xi–1 − Sqrt(C))2 / (2 Xi–1) < X0/2i . "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1776,"index":1776,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 6, end: 8 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"In particular, 0 ≤ Xm − Sqrt(C) < 1. If Sqrt(C) were an integer, then it would be equal to the floor of Xm . "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1777,"index":1777,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 8, end: 9 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"3. In general, the inequality Xi − Sqrt(C) < 1 will occur for values of i that are much less "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1778,"index":1778,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 9, end: 10 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"than m. To detect this, the fact that 2(m−1) ≤ Sqrt(C) < Xi for all i ≥ 1 can be used, "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1779,"index":1779,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 10, end: 13 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":" Xi − Sqrt(C) = ((Xi)2 − C)/( Xi + Sqrt(C))  ≤ ((Xi)2 − C)/( 2 Sqrt(C))  ≤ ((Xi)2 − C)/(2m) "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1780,"index":1780,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 13, end: 14 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"Thus, the condition (Xi)2 < 2m + C implies that Xi − Sqrt(C) < 1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1781,"index":1781,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 14, end: 15 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"C.5 Jacobi Symbol Algorithm "}
