ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1790,"index":1790,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 23, end: 24 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"result The calculated Jacobi symbol. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1791,"index":1791,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 24, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"Process: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1792,"index":1792,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 25, end: 26 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"1. a = a mod n. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1793,"index":1793,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 26, end: 27 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"Comment: a will be in the range 0 ≤ a < n. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1794,"index":1794,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(178), start: 27, end: 30 })","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"2. If a = 1, or n = 1, then return (1). 3. If a = 0, then return (0). 4. Define e and a1 such that a = 2e a1, where a1 is odd. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1795,"index":1795,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1796,"index":1796,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1797,"index":1797,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[85],"side":0,"text":"76 "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1798,"index":1798,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1799,"index":1799,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 1, end: 2 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"5. If e is even, then s = 1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1800,"index":1800,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 2, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"Else if ((n ≡ 1 (mod 8)) or (n ≡ 7 (mod 8))), then s = 1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1801,"index":1801,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 3, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"Else if ((n ≡ 3 (mod 8)) or (n ≡ 5 (mod 8)), then s = –1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1802,"index":1802,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 4, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"6. If ((n ≡ 3 (mod 4)) and (a1 ≡ 3 (mod 4))), then s = –s. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1803,"index":1803,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 5, end: 7 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"7. n1 = n mod a1. 8. Return (s * Jacobi (n1, a1)). Comment: Call this routine recursively. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1804,"index":1804,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 7, end: 8 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"Example: Compute the Jacobi symbol for a = 5 and n = 3439601197: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1805,"index":1805,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 8, end: 23 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"1. n is not 1, and a is not 1, so proceed to Step 2. 2. a is not 0, so proceed to Step 3. 3. 5 = 20 * 5, so e = 0, and a1 = 5. 4. e is even, so s = 1. 5. a1 is not congruent to 3 mod 4, so do not change s. 6. n1 = 2 = n mod 5. 7. Compute and return (1 * Jacobi(2, 5)). This calls Jacobi recursively. Compute the Jacobi symbol for a = 2 and n = 5: 7.1 n is not 1, and a is not 1, so proceed to Step 7.2. 7.2 a is not 0, so proceed to Step 7.3. 7.3 2 = 21 * 1, so e = 1, and a1 = 1. 7.4 e is odd, and n ≡ 5 (mod 8), so set s = –1. 7.5 n is not 3 mod 4, and a1 is not 3 mod 4, so proceed to step 7.6. 7.6 n1 = 0 = n mod 1. 7.7 Return (–1 * Jacobi(0, 1) = –1). This calls Jacobi recursively. Compute the Jacobi "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1806,"index":1806,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 23, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"symbol for a = 0 and n = 1: 7.7.1 n = 1, so return 1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1807,"index":1807,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 25, end: 26 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"Thus, Jacobi (0,1) = 1, so Jacobi (2,5) = –1*(1) = –1, and Jacobi (5, 3439601197) = 1* (–1) = –1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1808,"index":1808,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(179), start: 26, end: 27 })","issues":"[]","pages":[86],"side":0,"text":"C.6 Shawe-Taylor Random_Prime Routine "}
