ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1930,"index":1930,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(189), start: 4, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[92],"side":0,"text":"C.10 Construct a Provable Prime (possibly with Conditions), Based on "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1931,"index":1931,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(189), start: 5, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[92],"side":0,"text":"Contemporaneously Constructed Auxiliary Provable Primes "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1932,"index":1932,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(189), start: 6, end: 22 })","issues":"[]","pages":[92],"side":0,"text":"The following process (or its equivalent) shall be used to generate an L-bit provable prime p (a candidate for one of the prime factors of an RSA modulus). Note that the use of p in this specification is used generically; both RSA prime factors p and q may be generated using this method. If a so-called “strong prime” is required, this process can generate primes p1 and p2 (of specified bit-lengths N1 and N2) that divide p−1 and p+1, respectively. The resulting prime p will satisfy the conditions traditionally required of a strong prime, provided that the requested bit-lengths for p1 and p2 have appropriate sizes. Regardless of the bit-lengths selected for p1 and p2, the quantity p−1 will have a prime divisor p0 whose bit-length is slightly more than half that of p. In addition, the quantity p0 −1 will have a prime divisor whose bit-length is slightly more than half that of p0. This algorithm requires that N1 + N2 ≤ L – L/2 – 4. Values for N1 and N2 should be chosen such that N1 + N2 ≤ (L/2) – log2(L) – 7, to ensure that the algorithm can generate as many as 5L distinct candidates for p. Let Hash be the selected hash function to be used, and let outlen be the bit length of the hash function output block. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1933,"index":1933,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(189), start: 22, end: 23 })","issues":"[]","pages":[92],"side":0,"text":"Provable_Prime_Construction(): "}
