ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2049,"index":2049,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 20, end: 21 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2050,"index":2050,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 21, end: 22 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"D.1.1.3 Choice of Basis for Binary Fields "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2051,"index":2051,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 22, end: 24 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"To describe the arithmetic of a binary field, it is first necessary to specify how a bit string is to be interpreted. This is referred to as choosing a basis for the field. There are two common types of "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2052,"index":2052,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 24, end: 25 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"bases: a polynomial basis and a normal basis. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2053,"index":2053,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 25, end: 26 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"• A polynomial basis is specified by an irreducible polynomial modulo 2, called the field "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2054,"index":2054,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 26, end: 27 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"polynomial. The bit string (am–1 … a2 a1 a0) is taken to represent the polynomial "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2055,"index":2055,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 27, end: 28 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"am–1 t m–1 + …+ a2 t2 + a1 t + a0 "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2056,"index":2056,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 28, end: 30 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"over GF(2). The field arithmetic is implemented as polynomial arithmetic modulo p(t), where p(t) is the field polynomial. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2057,"index":2057,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 30, end: 32 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"• A normal basis is specified by an element θ of a particular kind. The bit string (a0 a1 a2  … am–1) is taken to represent the element "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2058,"index":2058,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 32, end: 33 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"a0θ + a1θ 2 + a2θ 2 2 + … + am–1θ 2 m–1 . "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2059,"index":2059,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 33, end: 36 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"Normal basis field arithmetic is not easy to describe or efficient to implement in general, except for a special class called Type T low-complexity normal bases. For a given field degree m, the choice of T specifies the basis and the field arithmetic (see Appendix D.3). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2060,"index":2060,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 36, end: 38 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"There are many polynomial bases and normal bases from which to choose. The following procedures are commonly used to select a basis representation. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2061,"index":2061,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 38, end: 39 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"• Polynomial Basis: If an irreducible trinomial tm + tk + 1 exists over GF (2), then the field "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2062,"index":2062,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(198), start: 39, end: 45 })","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"polynomial p(t) is chosen to be the irreducible trinomial with the lowest-degree middle term tk . If no irreducible trinomial exists, then a pentanomial t m + t a + t b + t c + 1 is selected. The particular pentanomial chosen has the following properties: the second term ta has the lowest degree m; the third term tb has the lowest degree among all irreducible pentanomials of degree m and second term ta; and the fourth term tc has the lowest degree among all irreducible pentanomials of degree m, second term ta, and third term tb. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2063,"index":2063,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2064,"index":2064,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2065,"index":2065,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[97],"side":0,"text":"88 "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2066,"index":2066,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2067,"index":2067,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 1, end: 2 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"• Normal Basis: Choose the Type T low-complexity normal basis with the smallest T. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2068,"index":2068,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 2, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"For each binary field, the parameters are given for the above basis representations. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2069,"index":2069,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 3, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"D.1.1.4 Choice of Curves "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2070,"index":2070,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 4, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"Two kinds of curves are given: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2071,"index":2071,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 5, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"• Pseudo-random curves are those whose coefficients are generated from the output of a "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2072,"index":2072,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 6, end: 9 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"seeded cryptographic hash function. If the domain parameter seed value is given along with the coefficients, it can be easily verified that the coefficients were generated by that method. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2073,"index":2073,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 9, end: 10 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"• Special curves are those whose coefficients and underlying field have been selected to "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2074,"index":2074,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 10, end: 11 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"optimize the efficiency of the elliptic curve operations. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2075,"index":2075,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 11, end: 12 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"For each curve size range, the following curves are given: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2076,"index":2076,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 12, end: 15 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"→ A pseudo-random curve over GF(p). → A pseudo-random curve over GF(2m). → A special curve over GF(2m) called a Koblitz curve or anomalous binary curve. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2077,"index":2077,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 15, end: 16 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"The pseudo-random curves were generated as specified in ANS X9.62 using SHA-1. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2078,"index":2078,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(199), start: 16, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[98],"side":0,"text":"D.1.1.5 Choice of Base Points "}
