ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":2518,"index":2518,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(225), start: 3, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[117],"side":0,"text":"The following algorithm computes the scalar multiple nP on the Koblitz curve Ea over GF(2m). The average number of elliptic additions and subtractions is at most ∼ 1 + (m/3), and is at most ∼ m/3 with probability at least 1 – 25–C. "}
