ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":221,"index":221,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(24), start: 1, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[12],"side":1,"text":"A cryptographic key that is used with an asymmetric (public key) cryptographic algorithm. The private key is uniquely associated with the owner and is not made public. The private key is used to compute a digital signature that may be verified using the corresponding public key. "}
