ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":364,"index":364,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(35), start: 1, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[16],"side":1,"text":"The ceiling of a: the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to a. For example, 5 = 5, 5.3 = 6, and –2.1 = –2. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":365,"index":365,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(35), start: 3, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[16],"side":1,"text":"The floor of a; the largest integer that is less than or equal to a. For example, 5 = 5, 5.3 = 5, and –2.1 = −3. "}
