ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":501,"index":501,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(61), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[26],"side":1,"text":"(d) Only two prime factors p and q shall be used to form the modulus n = pq. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":502,"index":502,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(61), start: 1, end: 2 })","issues":"[]","pages":[26],"side":1,"text":"(g) For RSASSA-PSS, the length (in bytes) of the salt (sLen) shall satisfy 0 ≤ sLen ≤ hLen, "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":503,"index":503,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(61), start: 2, end: 7 })","issues":"[]","pages":[26],"side":1,"text":"where hLen is the length of the hash function output block (in bytes). This inequality shall also be checked during the signature verification process, where hLen is determined by the expected (approved) hash function, and sLen is the actual byte length of the byte string following the leftmost (most significant) nonzero byte (which should be 0x01) in the recovered DB. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":504,"index":504,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(61), start: 7, end: 8 })","issues":"[]","pages":[26],"side":1,"text":"(h) For RSASSA-PKCS-v1.5, when the hash value is recovered from the encoded message "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":505,"index":505,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(61), start: 8, end: 10 })","issues":"[]","pages":[26],"side":1,"text":"EM during the verification of the digital signature,7 the extraction of the ASN.1 value of the DigestInfo data structure shall be accomplished by either: "}
