ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":509,"index":509,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"FIPS 186-5 "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":510,"index":510,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 1, end: 2 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"DIGITAL SIGNATURE STANDARD (DSS) "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":511,"index":511,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 2, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":512,"index":512,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 3, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"• Selecting the appropriate number of rightmost (least significant) bits of EM, as "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":513,"index":513,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 4, end: 9 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"determined by the size of a PKCS #1-defined ASN.1 DER value corresponding to the expected hash function’s algorithm identifier and output length, regardless of the length of the padding, Or (if the DigestInfo is selected by its location with respect to the last byte of padding), "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":514,"index":514,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 9, end: 10 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"• Checking that a byte string of the length expected for the ASN.1 DER value of "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":515,"index":515,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 10, end: 12 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"DigestInfo fills the remaining rightmost (least significant) bytes of EM (i.e., no other information follows the DigestInfo data structure in the encoded message). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":516,"index":516,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 12, end: 15 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"Only if the extracted DigestInfo has the appropriate form shall the signature verification process continue. Assuming that this is the case, the following two checks shall be performed:  "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":517,"index":517,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 15, end: 16 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"1. The algorithm identifier extracted from DigestInfo shall be examined to verify "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":518,"index":518,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 16, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"that the expected (approved) hash function has been identified. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":519,"index":519,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 17, end: 18 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"2. The length of the digest value that is extracted from DigestInfo shall be "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":520,"index":520,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 18, end: 21 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"determined and verified to be equal to the length of hash values output by the expected hash function.  "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":521,"index":521,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 21, end: 27 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"Only upon successful verification of both the algorithm identifier and the length of the digest value shall the extracted digest value be used as the recovered hash value during the verification of the digital signature.  Note that PKCS #1 was initially developed by RSA Laboratories in 1991 and has been revised as multiple versions. This standard references version 2.2 as published in IETF RFC 8017. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":522,"index":522,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(62), start: 27, end: 28 })","issues":"[]","pages":[27],"side":1,"text":"5.4.1 Mask Generation Functions in RSASSA-PSS "}
