ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":620,"index":620,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(76), start: 2, end: 7 })","issues":"[]","pages":[33],"side":1,"text":" Note that in the case of deterministic ECDSA, if r = 0 or s = 0, then generating a new permessage secret k will again lead to the same values for r and s. Statistically, this is extremely unlikely to happen. However, should it occur, the signature generation algorithm aborts and outputs failure. "}
