ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":658,"index":658,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"1. Interpret the octet string as an integer in little-endian representation. The most significant "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":659,"index":659,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 1, end: 2 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"2. To recover the x-coordinate, the curve equation requires x2 = (y2 – 1) / (d y2 – a) mod p. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":660,"index":660,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 2, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"The denominator is always non-zero mod p. Compute a square root to obtain x. Square roots can be computed using the Tonelli-Shanks algorithm (see NIST SP 800-186, Appendix E). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":661,"index":661,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 5, end: 7 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"The following routines describe simplified cases to compute square roots for p ≡ 3 mod 4 or p ≡ 5 mod 8. Let u = y2 – 1 and v = d y2 – a. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":662,"index":662,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 7, end: 8 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"a) To find a square root of (u/v) if p ≡ 3 mod 4 (as in Ed448), first compute the candidate "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":663,"index":663,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 8, end: 10 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"root w = (u/v) (p+1)/4 = u3 v (u5v3) (p-3)/4 mod p. If v w2 = u, the square root is x = w. Otherwise, no square root exists for modulo p, and the decoding fails. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":664,"index":664,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 10, end: 11 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"b) To find a square root of (u/v) if p ≡ 5 mod 8 (as in Ed25519), first compute the "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":665,"index":665,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(82), start: 11, end: 13 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"candidate root w = (u/v) (p+3)/8 = u v3 (u v7) (p-5)/8 mod p. To find the root, check three cases: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":666,"index":666,"interval":"None","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"•• IOf tvh ewr2w i=s e–,- un om soqdu apr, et hreo ostq euxairset sr ofootr ism ox d=u lwo p×, 2a(n(pd- 1)d/4e)c. oding fails. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":667,"index":667,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(83), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"• If v w2 = u mod p, the square root is x = w. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":668,"index":668,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(83), start: 1, end: 3 })","issues":"[]","pages":[35],"side":1,"text":"For both cases, if x = 0 and x0 = 1, point decoding fails. If x mod 2 = x0, then the x-coordinate is x. Otherwise, the x-coordinate is p – x. "}
