ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":782,"index":782,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(90), start: 3, end: 5 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"1. The primes p1, p2, q1, q2, p, and q shall all be provable primes (see Appendix A.1.4); "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":783,"index":783,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(90), start: 5, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"2. The primes p1, p2, q1, and q2 shall be provable primes, and the primes p and q "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":784,"index":784,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(90), start: 6, end: 7 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"shall be probable primes (see Appendix A.1.5); or "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":785,"index":785,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(90), start: 7, end: 9 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"3 The primes p1, p2, q1, q2, p, and q shall all be probable primes (see Appendix A.1.6). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":786,"index":786,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(90), start: 9, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"The minimum lengths for each of the auxiliary primes p1, p2, q1, and q2 are dependent on nlen, where nlen is the length of the modulus n in bits. Note that nlen is also called the key size. The lengths of the auxiliary primes may be fixed or randomly chosen, subject to the restrictions in Table A.1. The maximum length is determined by nlen (the sum of the length of each auxiliary prime pair) and whether the primes p and q are probable primes or provable primes (e.g., for the auxiliary prime pair p1 and p2, len(p1) + len(p2) shall be less than a value determined by nlen whether p1 and p2 are generated to be probable or provable primes).9 "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":787,"index":787,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(90), start: 17, end: 18 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"Table A.1. Minimum and maximum lengths of p1, p2, q1, and q2 "}
