ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":802,"index":802,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 10, end: 11 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"≤ 1005 bits "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":803,"index":803,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 11, end: 16 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":" For different values of nlen (i.e., different key sizes), random primes or primes with conditions are methods allowed for the generation of p and q. In addition, all IFC keys shall meet the following criteria in order to conform to this standard, FIPS 186-5: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":804,"index":804,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 16, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"1. The public exponent e shall be selected with the following constraints: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":805,"index":805,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 17, end: 18 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"(a) The public verification exponent e shall be selected prior to generating the "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":806,"index":806,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 18, end: 19 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"primes, p and q, and the private signature exponent d. "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":807,"index":807,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 19, end: 20 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":" "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":808,"index":808,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(91), start: 20, end: 26 })","issues":"[]","pages":[42],"side":1,"text":"9 For the probable primes p and q, len(p1) + len(p2) < len(p) – log2(len(p)) – 6, and similarly for len(q1) + len(q2) and len(q). For the provable primes p and q, len(p1) + len(p2) < len(p)/2 – log2(len(p)) – 7, and similarly for len(q1) + len(q2) and len(q). In each case, len(p) = len(q) = nlen/2. 10 If the constructed probable prime is being chosen to satisfy the (optional) additional c mod 8 requirement, then the size restriction on the maximum length of len(p1)+len(p2) is slightly less. The corresponding entries of this column become 1004 bits, 1515 bits, and 2027 bits, respectively. See Appendix B.9. "}
