ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":832,"index":832,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(92), start: 26, end: 32 })","issues":"[]","pages":[43],"side":1,"text":"An approved method that satisfies the constraints of Appendix A.1.1 shall be used for the generation of IFC random primes p and q that are provably prime (see case A.1). One such method is provided in Appendices A.1.2.1 and A.1.2.2. For this method, a random seed is initially required (see Appendix A.1.2.1); the length of the seed is equal to twice the security strength associated with the modulus n. After the seed is obtained, the primes can be generated (see Appendix A.1.2.2). "}
