ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1237,"index":1237,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(119), start: 3, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":1,"text":"Appendix B: Generation of Other Quantities "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1238,"index":1238,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(119), start: 4, end: 16 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":1,"text":"This appendix contains routines for the supplementary processes required for the implementation of this standard. Appendix B.1 is needed to produce the inverse of the per-message secret k (see Section 6.3 and Appendices A.2.1 and A.2.2) and the inverse of the signature portion s that is used during signature verification (see Section 6.4). The routines in Appendix B.2 are required to convert between bit strings and integers when implementing this standard. Appendix B.3 contains probabilistic primality tests to be used during the generation of RSA key pairs. Appendices B.4 and B.5 contain algorithms required during the Lucas probabilistic primality test of Appendix B.3.3 to check for a perfect square and to compute the Jacobi symbol. Appendix B.6 contains the Shawe-Taylor algorithm for the construction of primes. Appendix B.7 provides a process to perform trial division as required by the random prime generation routine in Appendix B.6. The sieve procedure in Appendix C.8 is needed by the trial division routine in Appendix B.7. The trial division process in Appendix B.7 and the sieve procedure in Appendix "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1239,"index":1239,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(119), start: 16, end: 17 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":1,"text":"B.8 have been extracted from ANS X9.80 [23], Prime Number Generation, Primality Testing, and "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1240,"index":1240,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(119), start: 17, end: 20 })","issues":"[]","pages":[61],"side":1,"text":"Primality Certificates. Appendix B.9 is required during the generation of RSA key pairs. Appendix B.10 provides a method for constructing provable primes for RSA (see Appendix A.1.2.2 and A.1.4). "}
