ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1558,"index":1558,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(144), start: 0, end: 1 })","issues":"[]","pages":[73],"side":1,"text":"To prove that c is prime: "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1559,"index":1559,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(144), start: 1, end: 4 })","issues":"[]","pages":[73],"side":1,"text":"is composite and exit. If convenient, c may be divided by composite numbers. For example, rather than preparing a table of primes, it might be more convenient to divide by all integers except those divisible by 3 or 5 (and then check if c is divisible by 3 or 5). "}
ISSUE12_BLOCK {"id":1560,"index":1560,"interval":"Some(TrustedRunInterval { run_id: TrustedRunId(144), start: 4, end: 6 })","issues":"[]","pages":[73],"side":1,"text":" Alternatively, rather than checking if an integer n divides c, computing GCD(n, c) may be more efficient. "}
