ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1511,1512,1513,1514,1515],"index":372,"kind":"Trusted(TrustedRunId(144))","side":0,"tokens":" 3. requested_security_strength = the security strength associated with N; see SP 800-57, Part 1. 4. Obtain a string of N returned_bits from an RBG with a security strength of requested_security_strength or more. If an ERROR indication is returned, then return an ERROR indication, Invalid_k, and Invalid_k_inverse. 5. Convert returned_bits to the (non-negative) integer c (see Appendix C.2.1). 6. If (c > n–2), then go to step 4. 7. k = c + 1. 8. (status, k–1) = inverse(k, n). 9. Return status, k, andk−1. "}
