ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[567],"index":395,"kind":"Untrusted(567)","side":1,"tokens":"6.2 Private/Public Keys "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[568],"index":396,"kind":"Untrusted(568)","side":1,"tokens":"An ECDSA or deterministic ECDSA key pair consists of a private key d and a public key Q, which are associated with a specific set of domain parameters (i.e., d, Q, and the domain parameters are mathematically related to each other). The private key is normally used for a period of time (i.e., the cryptoperiod); the public key may continue to be used as long as digital signatures that have been generated using the associated private key need to be verified (i.e., the public key may continue to be used beyond the cryptoperiod of the associated private key). See SP 800-57, Part 1, for further guidance. (Deterministic) ECDSA keys shall only be used for the generation and verification of (deterministic) ECDSA digital signatures. "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[569],"index":397,"kind":"Untrusted(569)","side":1,"tokens":"6.2.1 Key Pair Generation "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[570],"index":398,"kind":"Untrusted(570)","side":1,"tokens":"A digital signature key pair d and Q is generated for a set of domain parameters (q, FR, h, n, Type, a, b, G, {domain_parameter_seed}). Methods for the generation of d and Q are provided in Appendix A.2. "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[571],"index":399,"kind":"Untrusted(571)","side":1,"tokens":"6.2.2 Key Pair Management "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[572],"index":400,"kind":"Untrusted(572)","side":1,"tokens":"The secure use of digital signatures depends on the management of an entity’s digital signature key pair as specified in Section 5.2. Moreover, there are three additional requirements that pertain to ECDSA: "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[573],"index":401,"kind":"Untrusted(573)","side":1,"tokens":"1. The validity of the domain parameters shall be assured prior to the generation of the key "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[574],"index":402,"kind":"Untrusted(574)","side":1,"tokens":"pair or the verification and validation of a digital signature (see Section 3). "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[575],"index":403,"kind":"Untrusted(575)","side":1,"tokens":"2. Each key pair shall be associated with the domain parameters under which the key pair was generated. "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[576],"index":404,"kind":"Untrusted(576)","side":1,"tokens":"3. A key pair shall only be used to generate and verify signatures using the domain parameters associated with that key pair. "}
