ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[716],"index":521,"kind":"Untrusted(716)","side":1,"tokens":"7.8 The Prehash Edwards-Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (HashEdDSA) "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[717],"index":522,"kind":"Untrusted(717)","side":1,"tokens":"The Prehash Edwards-Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (HashEdDSA) is a version of the EdDSA digital signature scheme. The main difference is that HashEdDSA generates a signature on the hash of the message M, unlike EdDSA which signs the message M directly. The domain parameters and key generation for HashEdDSA are exactly the same as for EdDSA with the two options denoted Ed25519ph and Ed448ph. Below are the signature generation and verification processes for Ed25519ph and Ed448ph. Section 7.8.3 explains potential reasons for choosing between HashEdDSA and EdDSA. "}
