ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1149],"index":888,"kind":"Untrusted(1149)","side":1,"tokens":"This method uses a cryptographically strong DRBG to produce a random bit string that has the same bit-size as the requested random integer k in the interval [1, n−1]. The value of k in the requested range is determined by this bit string. This non-deterministic procedure removes bias in practice. In this method, a random number is obtained and tested to determine that it will produce a value of k in the correct range. If k is out of range, an ERROR is returned. The following procedure or its equivalent may be used to generate a random integer per-message secret number in the interval [1, n −1]. "}
