ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1801],"index":1445,"kind":"Untrusted(1801)","side":1,"tokens":"• ANSI X9.31 was withdrawn, so X9.31 RSA signatures were removed from this standard. • ANSI X9.62 was removed, so new specifications for ECDSA were added to FIPS 186-5. "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1802],"index":1446,"kind":"Untrusted(1802)","side":1,"tokens":"Note: X9.62 will be replaced by X9.142 (under development). "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1803],"index":1447,"kind":"Untrusted(1803)","side":1,"tokens":"• Many elliptic curve details and algorithms from FIPS 186-4 will now be included in SP 800-186. "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1804],"index":1448,"kind":"Untrusted(1804)","side":1,"tokens":"o dEellpirpeticca tceudr. ves defined over binary curves (specified in SP 800-186) are now "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1805],"index":1449,"kind":"Untrusted(1805)","side":1,"tokens":"• A new deterministic signature algorithm, EdDSA, is included, as is the prehash version. • A deterministic version of ECDSA is specified. • Larger modulus sizes are allowed for RSA (with updated tables A.1, B.1). • XOFs are allowed for use in ECDSA, RSASSA-PSS. • Constructing primes with congruence conditions mod 8 is allowed. • In B.3.1, the two most significant bits of p and q may be set arbitrarily. • Trial division before checking primality is allowed. • Updated algorithms are included in Appendices B and C to better prevent bias. • The option to generate elliptic curves (besides those specified in SP 800-186) is removed. "}
ISSUE12_VIEW {"blocks":[1806],"index":1450,"kind":"Untrusted(1806)","side":1,"tokens":"Similarly, users are not given the option to generate their own base points on elliptic curves. "}
